WEBVTT

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:33.220
What a childish prank.

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:39.020
Still, they've never come directly to
the house to antagonize me before...

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:42.440
There were those guys
snoopin' about our yard...

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:48.280
It must've been them!

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:51.360
Uncle, please, stay calm.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.660
If you let your rage consume you
and turn to violence,

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:57.200
that will only give them
a reason to escalate.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.710
I understand how you feel,
but we shouldn't retaliate--

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:05.960
Don't you worry.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:10.090
I know my hair-trigger temper
not only lead me down a shitty life,

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:16.930
but it hurt the family
I love so damn much.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:19.310
I was such a moron.

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:28.020
Yes, you certainly were.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:34.360
Maebara-<i>san</i>... You're the boss.
Want to kick things off?

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.450
Thank you so much for coming here today!

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:43.920
Satoko Hojo has been locked in her house
by her uncle for several days now!

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.540
The same uncle who physically abused her
then abandoned her for a year!

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:50.590
How is he fit to be her "guardian"?!

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:56.140
We can't stand by and watch
Satoko-<i>chan </i>suffer any more!

00:01:56.140 --> 00:02:01.270
But look at this crowd!
We'll show CWS how much we care!

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:04.350
We're not going to abandon one of our own!

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:07.810
This is our third straight day
of petitioning CWS,

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:11.360
and we're going to go in there and
tell them to handle her case immediately!

00:03:56.210 --> 00:04:01.010
HIGURASHI: WHEN THEY CRY SOTSU

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.790
How'd it go, Kei-<i>chan</i>?

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:31.880
Felt like a repeat of yesterday.

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:34.630
So they're just gonna
keep "monitoring" her?

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:39.090
Yes, and they'll make
a decision in a month's time.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:43.720
A month?! Who knows how much permanent
damage Satoko will suffer in a month!

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:47.470
At the very least, they did
seem to take us seriously...

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:50.560
We told everyone
we'd be back at this tomorrow,

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:53.730
but we might lose a few people.

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:55.440
This is so frustrating.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:05:00.150
Even if nobody shows,
I'm not going to back down!

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.780
Neither will I.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:06.370
If we don't work together,
we can't make miracles happen.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:07.540
That's right.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:08.700
Yeah!

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:21.500
"Watanagashi Festival Planning Meeting"

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:25.300
Look, the dam war ended ages ago!

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:28.970
It's done and over, as are the days
of bandin' together and protesting!

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:33.650
I'm not talking about "those days"
or the dam war or anything!

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:36.190
I'm talking about the war
I'm fighting right now!

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:39.900
You should watch your tongue!

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:41.900
Young people these days!

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:47.160
All right. Let's see what you've got.

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:49.370
Let's just be honest here.

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:53.040
You're afraid there are people here
who are against helping out the Hojos.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:54.750
Isn't that right?

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:56.750
I see.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:06:03.050
Maebara-<i>san </i>really believes
he's doing the right thing here.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:08.010
And now that his friends
have duped him into believing that...

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:11.930
...he's taking part in the harassment
without realizing it at all.

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:14.140
He thinks he's protecting Satoko-<i>san</i>,

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:16.690
when really, he's trying to tear her away
from her only surviving family

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:20.400
which will hurt her even more.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:24.910
How would he react if he knew the truth?

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:28.240
And the village is using
the Hojos as an excuse

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:33.330
to get fired up and band together again,
just like they did in the good old days.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:39.090
You're proving to be a very useful pawn
for the culprits behind the curse.

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:43.840
You're not half bad, Maebara-<i>san</i>.

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:50.810
Yesterday's got nothing on today's crowd.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:54.810
The whole village responded
to his call to action.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:07:00.690
At least, it would seem so on the surface.

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:02.440
Only on the surface?

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:05.740
It's all going according to
the village's grand scheme.

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:09.200
Still, he's shaping up to be
a future Hinamizawa bigshot.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:14.870
You might want to get on good terms
with him as soon as you can, Kuma-<i>chan</i>.

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:24.130
Where are you going?

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:29.010
Next spring, I'll finally be
old enough to retire.

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:33.470
Better go make the chief
look good while I can.

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:37.390
Is that...

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:41.310
Maebara-<i>san</i>! Hello there!

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:47.030
Sir...

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:49.820
I'll give the Okinomiya PD another call!

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:52.780
Right, I'll get him.

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:58.540
Ooishi-<i>san</i>!

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:00.880
The chief's trying to radio you.

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:02.710
Oh, thank you.

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:05.760
I need to step away for a moment.

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:09.260
I'd appreciate it if you all got
to dispersing this crowd.

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:16.310
Ooishi-<i>san</i>... I knew you were
going easy on them.

00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:18.310
You're so quick to use force,

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:22.270
the second you tried to talk it out,
I knew something was up.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:27.320
We'll let Maebara-<i>san</i>
take all the credit today.

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:30.740
Want a smoke?

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:40.170
Maebara-<i>san </i>doesn't doubt for a second
that he's doing the right thing.

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:41.580
What'd you say?

00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:46.960
Now's the time to let <i>him </i>be the star
and for <i>us </i>to play a little pretend.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:47.960
Huh?

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:50.430
Oh, my.

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:53.140
Here they are.

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:55.560
Let's go, Kuma-<i>chan</i>.

00:08:59.270 --> 00:09:01.140
I know them!

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:06.190
How's it look down there?
Are they going to disperse?

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:12.780
O-Ooishi-<i>san </i>is talking to them right now.

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:19.290
What happened?!

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:21.080
They're coming in!

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:23.830
Okay, everyone! We're going in!

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:30.300
We're almost there, Satoko!

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:37.680
Now that smells damn good!

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:41.690
I can assure you, it tastes good, too!

00:09:41.690 --> 00:09:44.060
Be a dear and set the table, will you?

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:45.980
I'm on it!

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:56.030
I'm so sorry for the trouble!

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:58.990
So you're gonna do something
to help her right away, yeah?

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:00.200
Of course!

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:02.750
Assistant Manager!
Head straight to the Hojo residence!

00:10:02.750 --> 00:10:05.040
Wait, me?

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:06.790
Shouldn't we speak
with their social worker--

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:10.210
Please, she doesn't have much time!

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:12.170
O-Okay! I'll head out right away!

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:15.390
It's almost time for us
to move out, Kuma-<i>chan</i>.

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:20.680
If we don't do something, they may
very well scare Teppei out of the village.

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:23.440
Wait, is that a bad thing?

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:28.650
It would be. I need him to stick around
at least until Watanagashi.

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:34.610
Hold on a second, there.

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:37.280
You're not gonna try
to stop us again, are you?

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:38.910
Not at all.

00:10:38.910 --> 00:10:40.450
Harayama-<i>san</i>!

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:44.000
If you're heading towards the Hojos,
then let me take you there.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:44.620
Huh?

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:46.170
Are you sure?

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:51.420
Satoko-<i>chan</i>'s uncle will have to
let them in if they show up with the cops.

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:52.340
You're right.

00:10:52.340 --> 00:10:56.010
But why the change of heart,
Detective Ooishi?

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:03.060
I want CWS to understand
how horrific the Hojo situation is.

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:05.980
Seeing it first-hand's
the best way to do that.

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:08.400
All right. Thanks for the help.

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:11.020
Okay, Harayama-<i>san</i>, this way, please.

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:16.700
Oh, right! Could you all disperse now?

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:29.380
Teppei Hojo-<i>san </i>and Satoko-<i>san</i>, I presume?

00:11:29.380 --> 00:11:33.550
My name is Harayama, and I'm from
Okinomiya Child Welfare Services.

00:11:33.550 --> 00:11:35.130
Child Welfare Services?!

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:38.800
Dammit, Detective!
The hell is the meaning of this?!

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:40.800
I figured having them come by to see

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:46.020
the truth with their own eyes
would be faster than explaining it myself.

00:11:46.020 --> 00:11:48.850
What do you mean, "the truth"?

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:57.110
The village has banded together
to harass me and my uncle.

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:58.490
What?

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:12.340
You knew all this, Ooishi-<i>san</i>?

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:15.300
They came to me for help before.

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:17.220
Still, I can't believe it...

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:20.720
The whole village is really
working together to harass them?

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:26.890
Hinamizawa is the one place
where something this rotten could happen.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:34.650
I've done a thorough search of your home,
and interviewed Satoko-<i>san</i>.

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:36.530
And?

00:12:36.530 --> 00:12:39.200
To be perfectly honest,

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:43.370
your home situation is nothing like
what the protesters were declaring.

00:12:43.370 --> 00:12:45.040
That's what we've been tellin' ya!

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:51.670
Now, then, since you know the truth,
what will CWS be doing with the Hojos?

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:57.880
As someone born and raised in Okinomiya,
I know Hinamizawa is a <i>unique </i>place.

00:12:57.880 --> 00:13:03.140
And with the Sonozaki family involved,
I can't say I'm sure how to handle this.

00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:05.850
How about this, then?

00:13:05.850 --> 00:13:10.270
Transfer responsibility
of this case to me.

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:13.190
Hand it over to the police.

00:13:13.190 --> 00:13:15.650
Hold on, Ooishi-<i>san</i>!
We haven't even asked the chief if--

00:13:16.610 --> 00:13:18.360
What do you say?

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:24.530
Yes, that will do.
I leave it to you, then.

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:28.620
Smart choice.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:35.000
Come to think of it,
Watanagashi is tomorrow, isn't it?

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.170
What about it?

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:40.260
You're well aware of
Oyashiro-<i>sama</i>'s curse, yes?

00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:42.760
A curse that targets
the village's enemies...

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:44.550
isn't that right?

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:47.810
We're the village's enemies.

00:13:47.810 --> 00:13:48.890
That's right.

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:55.520
It's very likely that the criminals who
carry out that curse will come after you.

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:58.400
I'd recommend staying inside
all day tomorrow.

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:01.240
I-Is that enough to keep us safe?!

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:05.820
I'll keep watch over your house at night
when the festival's going on.

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:10.160
You'll be safe.

00:14:32.270 --> 00:14:33.390
Hello?!

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:35.310
Rika?

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:39.150
Are you okay?!
Did Ooishi and CWS come to your--

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:41.480
Calm down, please.

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:45.450
Keiichi-<i>san </i>asked me the very same thing
when I called him just now.

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:47.910
So what happened, then?

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:53.250
When I asked for help,
my uncle got angry and attacked me...

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:59.290
But Ooishi-<i>san </i>subdued him
and took him off to the police station.

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:04.300
Are you hurt?

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:11.010
I'm fine. And now, my uncle will
never return to this house ever again.

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:13.980
Good.

00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:16.310
I'm so glad you stood up and fought.

00:15:17.190 --> 00:15:20.360
You fought fate and won.

00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:22.650
Rika...

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:25.990
Now, I'll finally be free.

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:36.580
She probably thinks
she's found a nice happy ending.

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:40.670
But Oyashiro-<i>sama</i>'s curse
is only just beginning.

00:15:46.510 --> 00:15:49.970
So Satoko-<i>chan </i>can come
celebrate Watanagashi with us?!

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:50.720
Yeah!

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:53.720
She told me over the phone she's looking
forward to "thoroughly enjoying" it!

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:56.690
Sounds like Satoko-<i>chan</i>, all right.

00:15:56.690 --> 00:15:58.560
Hey, there they are!

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:02.520
Mii-<i>chan</i>, sorry we're late!

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:05.940
Ta-dah! Guess who's coming with you?

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:08.200
We're just missing those two now.

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:10.950
Rika-<i>chan </i>is going to pick Satoko up.

00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:12.990
Then the gang will be back together again!

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:14.660
Uh-huh!

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:18.000
Tonight's gonna be so special,
I just know it!

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:29.840
My, you're finally awake?

00:16:33.310 --> 00:16:35.640
My head's so heavy...

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:42.860
The hell is wrong...

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:53.240
Rika should be here very soon.
What terrible timing you have, Uncle.

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:59.330
I'm supposed to be a pitiful princess who
was just rescued from her horrible uncle.

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:02.460
And at the festival, everyone in
the village will worry about me,

00:17:02.460 --> 00:17:05.880
support me, and fawn over me.

00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:10.550
Satoko? You okay? Did somethin'
happen while I was passed out?

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:13.510
I thought the villagers were bullyin' ya.

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:17.520
Uncle.

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:19.060
Yeah?

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:24.480
What did you think of the time
we spent here together?

00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:30.360
It was nice.

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:34.120
A shithead like me
barely deserved to feel...

00:17:34.120 --> 00:17:36.330
...as happy as I did.

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:40.330
Well, I'm glad to hear it.

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:42.620
But that ends here.

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:47.800
S-Satoko?

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:51.510
It's time for you to die.

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:01.230
Huh?!

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:04.520
What the hell is happening?!

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:09.780
Uncle!

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:11.030
Run!

00:18:11.030 --> 00:18:14.570
What? I'm certainly not going
to let him get away!

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:22.040
Please, Uncle,

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:24.120
y-you have to run!

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:28.130
S-Satoko?! What's happenin' to you?!

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:37.970
Don't be a fool!

00:18:59.490 --> 00:19:01.200
Please, stop!

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:03.200
Have you lost your senses?!

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:06.790
I'm through with this!
I'm through with <i>all </i>of this!

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:10.420
I don't want to kill my Uncle!
I don't want to kill anyone else!

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:12.760
I don't want anyone else to die!

00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:18.390
I am living through these endless loops
to ensure Satoko Hojo's happiness!

00:19:18.390 --> 00:19:21.640
You're not me! You aren't <i>me </i>anymore!

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:24.730
Give me back! Give Satoko back to me!

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:25.940
Excuse me?

00:19:27.980 --> 00:19:29.770
Whatever are you saying?

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:32.280
I am Satoko.

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:44.500
So what does that make you?

00:19:44.500 --> 00:19:48.880
You claim to be Satoko, but you are merely
the leavings of an old fragment!

00:19:48.880 --> 00:19:49.880
No, I'm not!

00:19:49.880 --> 00:19:53.630
Yes, you certainly are.
Give me back to you?

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:56.220
I am Satoko Hojo!

00:19:56.220 --> 00:19:57.930
It's high time you ceased to exist!

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:05.430
I don't know where I went wrong...

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:07.770
But I went wrong <i>somewhere</i>!

00:20:07.770 --> 00:20:09.480
I love Rika!

00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:11.820
I love Rika so much!

00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:14.570
I want to be with Rika forever!

00:20:14.570 --> 00:20:18.110
I just learned to be honest
about that love, that's all!

00:20:19.410 --> 00:20:22.240
But I must've gone wrong somewhere.

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:25.120
So you <i>can't </i>be right!

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:32.540
From my perspective,

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:38.220
<i>you </i>went wrong when your outdated
emotions rejected this current reality.

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:41.720
I am Satoko Hojo.

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:47.140
I am one who lives in loops. One who
traverses the great sea of fragments.

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:49.690
Indeed, I am a <i>witch</i>.

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:03.740
Eua-<i>san</i>?

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:04.830
Your tale--

00:21:04.830 --> 00:21:10.830
nay, your <i>shared </i>tale is so
unfathomably entertaining!

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:15.460
Lending you my power
was truly an apt decision!

00:21:17.510 --> 00:21:19.670
You... You knew,

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:21.720
from the very beginning...

00:21:21.720 --> 00:21:25.180
I will say, though you
happily received my power,

00:21:25.180 --> 00:21:28.810
your manner of speaking
was somewhat unpleasant at times.

00:21:28.810 --> 00:21:34.270
Even so, this has all been
<i>quite </i>amusing, Satoko.

00:21:38.030 --> 00:21:41.400
If your current state brings you anguish,

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:47.830
then to reward you, I shall relieve you
of those emotions forevermore.

00:21:53.460 --> 00:21:56.250
You are so truly entertaining!

00:22:01.760 --> 00:22:04.140
I was so stupid.

00:22:04.140 --> 00:22:08.100
My, I'm not stupid in the slightest.

00:22:18.020 --> 00:22:19.860
Satoko...?

00:23:42.900 --> 00:23:46.910
Next time: "Tatariakashi-hen:
Curse Revealing Chapter, Part 5."
